(Title) Tj
T*
(Expanded tuberculosis diagnostic algorithms for hospitalized HIV-positive patients: a) Tj
T*
(pragmatic randomized trial protocol) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Rationale: Tuberculosis remains the leading cause of mortality in hospitalized persons) Tj
T*
(with advanced HIV. Standard symptom-triggered diagnostic approaches may miss TB in) Tj
T*
(atypical presentations. This protocol describes a pragmatic trial evaluating expanded) Tj
T*
(diagnostic strategies. Methods: Hospitalized adults with HIV \(>=18 years, no prior TB) Tj
T*
(diagnosis or recent treatment\) will be enrolled within 24 hours of admission across 11) Tj
T*
(hospitals in Tanzania and Mozambique \(target n=1200\). Participants will be randomly) Tj
T*
(assigned 1:1 to expanded diagnostic arm or standard-care arm. Expanded arm receives TB) Tj
T*
(testing from sputum, stool, and urine specimens plus urine antigen testing, irrespective) Tj
T*
(of symptoms. Standard arm receives symptom-based WHO-recommended sputum and urine antigen) Tj
T*
(testing. All participants receive medical management per standard protocols. Primary) Tj
T*
(outcome: proportion with microbiologically confirmed TB initiating treatment within 72) Tj
T*
(hours. Secondary outcomes: 8-week mortality, time from hospital admission to TB diagnosis,) Tj
T*
(and diagnostic yield by specimen type. Follow-up: all participants followed through 8) Tj
T*
(weeks post-enrollment for mortality and TB diagnosis outcomes. Blinding: laboratory) Tj
T*
(personnel blinded to diagnostic arm. Study design: pragmatic individually randomized) Tj
T*
(controlled trial.) Tj
ET
